The [#4471 page](/kb/incidents/4471) calls the ticket one issue with one fix queued. The reports
say otherwise. Read by what each body describes, and placed by each tenant's locale and booking
form, the ticket holds three problems. One fix will not close it.

<Callout kind="warn">
Not one issue. Three, each with its own ticket. The parser fix closed only the first.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} />

## The three problems

**`parser` — the shared parser reads dates month first.** Every tenant on file writes the day
first. Their dates come out with day and month swapped: 7 April becomes 4 July. This is the bug
the #4471 page describes, and the queued fix is for it.

**`hint` — the booking-v3 form asks for the wrong order.** booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under
its date field. People at day-first tenants type what the hint tells them, month first, and the
form reads it the tenant's way. The result looks like the parser bug, but the parser fix does
not touch it. Only form reports from booking-v3 tenants have it.

**`one-day` — invites land one whole day off.** These reports describe a shift by one day, not
a swap: Tuesday shows as Monday, an invite arrives before the booking, two clients in different
cities get different days for the same meeting. The desk already read them this way
(`desk-notes.json`) and filed them under `parser` by tenant, where they stay counted. A month/day
fix cannot move a date by one day, so this needs its own ticket.

## How it got merged

- Decision [0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on the subject line alone. All
  three problems use the same words ("wrong day", "date is wrong"), so subject matching put them
  in one ticket.
- Intake tags are a guess from the reporter's browser, and they disagree with the cause. Count
  by tenant, form and body, not by tag.
- The export repeats some reports. Count each id once.

## For comparison: the existing cause table

The table the #4471 page shows. It sees two causes, and only footnotes the one-day reports under `parser`.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## Outcome

Engineering closed #4471 on 5 October.

- `parser`: **fixed** by `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`. Ticket closed as completed.
- `hint`: **won't fix**. The booking-v3 form is retired, so no new reports can come in this way.
  Ticket closed as not planned.
- `one-day`: **no fix**. Neither change touches a one-day shift. Ticket closed as not planned; if
  the desk sees one-day reports again, reopen it rather than merge them into a date ticket.

## Next

- Re-check decision 0001: matching on subject merges different bugs that people describe alike.

